Modifications to derived material
---------------------------------

The following changes were made to the original BCM59111 driver. They are
listed because GPL-2.0 requires that modified versions carry prominent notices
stating that they were changed:

  - ported the i2c probe path to the device-tree based of_match_table flow
  - replaced __devinitdata, __devexit and remove_new, all removed upstream
  - class_create() lost its THIS_MODULE argument
  - CURRENT_TIME_SEC replaced with ktime_get_real_seconds()
  - sysfs permissions on power-control attributes tightened from 0222/0666 to
    0220/0664, because the driver exposes power control and world-writable
    attributes would let any local user cut power to attached devices
  - added a compatible with a device-tree node, so the controller is described
    in bcm958625-meraki-alamo.dtsi rather than by hardcoded register access

Because driver/bcm59111.c is a derivative work, it remains under GPL-2.0-only.


